## Extending the Project

Models and datasets are added to an existing project using the **mlops-cli** tool, not Copier. Copier only generates the initial scaffold; the CLI handles all subsequent onboarding.

### Add a New Model

```bash
mlops-cli add-model mlops_{{ project }}/ --model-name <new_model_name>
```

Generates per-model config YAMLs under each pipeline stage and adds the corresponding workflow job. After running, open each generated file and replace `<ds_project>` with the actual DS package name.

### Add a New Dataset

```bash
mlops-cli add-dataset mlops_{{ project }}/ --dataset-name <new_dataset_name>
```

Merges the new dataset's data extraction, preprocessing, featurization, and splitter/prepare_input actions into the existing training, inference, and retraining pipeline configs. After running, replace `<catalog.schema.table>` and `<data_science_module_file_path>` placeholders in the updated files.

### Remove a Model or Dataset

```bash
mlops-cli remove-model  mlops_{{ project }}/ --model-name <model_name>
mlops-cli remove-dataset mlops_{{ project }}/ --dataset-name <dataset_name>
```

